From 0d53b4b64802e1ead881bc1231413d165b1e1018 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexey Lapin <a.lapin03@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:10:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] feat(server): replay recorded first turns of booth demo
 chats

hone-pi starts the real Pi and passes its RPC through. When the first
message of a new chat, the model, the thinking level and the project
folder match a recording, it plays the recorded Pi events back at their
pace, writes the files the turn wrote and the Pi session file, sends the
session to Hone as the Hone extension does, and loads it into Pi. Anything
else runs live. HONE_TURN_CACHE_RECORD=1 records new first turns.

A replay leaves <session file>.hone-replay.json with its source.
